No, it wouldn't.  Jumping boots don't work in that sort of situation
and teleporting is impossible on the castle level. Rocks will work,
but they have to be *big* rocks (boulders). Since you would need five
of them, they're not really practical, unless you can reverse-genocide
stone giants or something.  You would need some method of levitating
(ring, boots, potion or spell) or boots of water walking.  I have also
heard that it is possible to dig through the top-most wall along the
moat, but I haven't verified this yet, and it may be just an unfounded
rumor.  The ball-and-chain solution is a novel concept, and rather
elegant, but not for characters with <18 strength, and you would have
to be very careful positioning yourself.

